 Use [testnet.cspr.trade](https://testnet.cspr.trade) to get wrapped CSPR (WCSPR) or csprUSD for
 the client payments.
 
+#### Ycash (regtest)
+
+Ycash testnet had no reachable seeds when this binding was written, so the Ycash family runs
+against a **regtest** node. Every role talks to it through `YCASH_RPC_URL`, which the harness
+fills from `YCASH_TESTNET_RPC_URL`.
+
+1. Start a regtest `ycashd` (a 4.5.0 or 6.21.0 build; YEC needs no Ycash-specific flag), with
+   Overwinter and Sapling active from block 1 as the node's own test harness does:
+   `ycashd -regtest -server -daemon -rpcuser=x402 -rpcpassword=x402 -rpcport=18232 -nuparams=5ba81b19:1 -nuparams=76b809bb:1`,
+   then mature some coinbase: `ycash-cli -regtest -rpcuser=x402 -rpcpassword=x402 -rpcport=18232 generate 101`.
+2. Make a payer key and fund it with several separate coins (one per scenario: a payment's change
+   is unconfirmed until the next block): `getnewaddress`, `dumpprivkey <addr>` → `CLIENT_YCASH_WIF`,
+   then `sendtoaddress <addr> 0.1` ten times and `generate 1`.
+3. Set `SERVER_YCASH_ADDRESS` to another `getnewaddress`, and
+   `YCASH_NETWORK=ycash:regtest`, `YCASH_TESTNET_RPC_URL=http://x402:x402@127.0.0.1:18232/`.
+
+The `/exact/ycash` route charges 0.001 YEC (`SERVER_YCASH_AMOUNT` overrides it). Payments up to
+`YCASH_ZERO_CONF_CAP_ZAT` (default 0.01 YEC) settle at the mempool, so no block is needed per
+payment. Once Ycash testnet has seeds again, leave `YCASH_NETWORK` unset and point
+`YCASH_TESTNET_RPC_URL` at a testnet node.
+
 #### Cardano Preprod
 
 1. Create a preprod wallet (CIP-30 wallet or `PrivateKey.generateMnemonic()` from `@evolution-sdk/evolution`) and set `CLIENT_CARDANO_MNEMONIC` plus `SERVER_CARDANO_ADDRESS` (the client's `addr_test1...` works).
